BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spicy Soiree: No Immigrants No Spice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639651@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerNo Immigrants No SpiceAn intim
 ate fundraiser featuring a dinner by Chef Reem Assil\, Yucatan-inspired bi
 tes from Chef Lorenzo Caamal\, live performances\, and a maker market.\nJo
 in No Immigrants No Spice\, Chef Reem Assil\, and Merkado for an unforgett
 able fundraiser celebrating the people\, stories\, and flavors that immigr
 ation brings to our communities.\n\nThe evening will include:\n️ An inti
 mate chef’s dinner from award-winning Palestinian-Syrian Chef Reem Assil
  of Reem’s California\nCreative bites and desserts from Executive Chef L
 orenzo Caamal\, Merkado\, drawing on his Yucatán roots and fresh Californ
 ia ingredients\nCraft cocktails by Merkado\nLive performances from Melissa
  Cruz\, Zedan & Osman\, and Diana Gameros featuring Raúl Vargas on cajón
 \nThoughtful programming to make invisible labor visible\, featuring immig
 rant speakers representing key areas of California’s economy and landsca
 pe.\n️ Our first-ever Spicy Soiree market featuring immigrant owned and 
 aligned makers\, artists\, and creators.\nNo Immigrants No Spice (NINS) is
  known for BBQ Without Borders\, bringing hundreds of people together arou
 nd food. The Spicy Soiree will be a bit different – a more intimate gath
 ering designed to spark connection and conversation around the table\, whi
 le raising funds for the NINS mission of shifting the narrative on immigra
 tion\, and making the 2027 BBQ Without Borders event possible.\nNote: we a
 re offering a reduced price “entertainment-only” ticket to expand acce
 ss to...\n\n$15.00\n\nTickets: https://events.humanitix.com/nins-spicy-soi
 ree\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/spicy-soiree-immigrants-spice/\nSour
 ce: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Spicy-
 Soiree-Event-Banner.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Merkado SF\, 130 Townsend Street\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/spicy-soiree-immigrants-spice/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queen Budapest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T210000
DTSTAMP:20261011T055613Z
UID:dothebay-17829783@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:On July 27\, 1986\, Queen performed the largest-ever stadium c
 oncert at the Népstadion in Budapest in front of 80\,000 ecstatic fans.\n
 \nThe concert was part of the famed Magic Tour\, which was the last time t
 he band toured with lead singer Freddie Mercury. Now\, this original conce
 rt film has been beautifully rescanned and remastered in 4K alongside a dy
 namic new audio mix\, featuring many of Queen's favorite tracks— "Bohemi
 an Rhapsody\,” "Crazy Little Thing Called Love\," "I Want To Break Free
 ” and "We Are The Champions."\n\nWith three years to go before the fall 
 of the Berlin Wall\, this was the first Western rock concert performed in 
 a stadium behind the then Iron Curtain. It was of such significance to the
  Hungarian authorities and film industry that a group of the country’s t
 op film cameramen and technicians were brought together to film it for pos
 terity.\n\nThis film can be used with loyalty cards or our 2026 annual Cin
 emaSF passes\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/queen-buda
 pest-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34363025/916a019f-1e0e-41a0-a5e5-5f2d2d9bc75b.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261011T055613Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/queen-budapest-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1633237@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)\n
 Lindy in the Park\nGet ready to swing in Golden Gate Park every sunny Sund
 ay at “Lindy in the Park\,” a weekly free event near the de Young Muse
 um\, when the streets of Golden Gate Park are closed to traffic and the da
 ncers take over.\nThis in person event resumed June 20\, 2021\nLindy in th
 e Park | Free Outdoor Swing Dance & Lessons\nEvery Sunday | 11 am to 2 pm\
 nJFK Dr. btwn 8th and 10th\, behind the De Young Museum\, Golden Gate Park
 \, SF\nFREE\nRain and Bay to Breakers cancels\, but other than that\, Lind
 y in the Park takes place every Sunday – even on holidays – so even if
  New Year’s Day\, Christmas\, or Fourth of July falls on a Sunday\, they
 ’ll be out there dancing. On the very rare occasion when they cancel\, t
 hey’ll make a new posting on their website\, usually by 10am on Sunday. 
 Lindy in the Park’s Schedule FAQ\n\nFree Beginners Swing Lessons | Noon 
 to 12:30 pm\nLindy in the Park offers a free weekly beginning swing dance 
 lesson\, taught by Hep Jen. The lessons are short\, easy and fun and then 
 you can practice your new steps with the whole group until 2 pm.\nNo partn
 er is required\, as they rotate leaders and followers throughout the lesso
 n.\nUpdated 7/8/2021 – Event info last checked via website.\n\nUpcoming 
