SUMMARY:“Lights On” SF’s Historic Broadway Sign Relighting + Sidewal
 k Party (North Beach)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T210000
DTSTAMP:20261013T225222Z
UID:funcheap-1642314@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Mabuhay GardensLights ON! marks the return of the restored BRO
 ADWAY sign at the former Mabuhay Gardens building in North Beach. The free
  sidewalk program includes remarks\, a dusk countdown and sign lighting\, 
 plus samples from Francesca’s Cafe. Ticketed upstairs programming at On 
 Broadway / Broadway Studios includes Michael Brunswick’s Live Canvas Art
  Performance\, live music by GamperDrums\, a Filipino American History Mon
 th tribute\, an exhibition preview\, a slideshow and tributes to Mabuhay G
 ardens.\nThe 6-7 PM sidewalk gathering and sign-lighting countdown are fre
 e with no ticket required. Upstairs admission from 7-9 PM starts at $5 for
  Community tickets\; General admission is $25\, with optional $50 Supporte
 r and $100 Sustaining Supporter tickets. Tickets include the same upstairs
  access and are limited to 200 guests. Existing bulb backers may register 
 upstairs for free while space remains.\nLocated in the heart of North Beac
 h at 435 Broadway near Kearny\, the classic Mission-style building was bui
 lt in 1919 by the Italian community and began its first incarnation as Gar
 ibaldi Hall. In the 1930s it was a favorite ballroom for swing and jazz ni
 ghts\, which saw the likes of Louis Armstrong grace its stage.\n\nIn the 
 ’70s the venue was host to many memorable events including appearances f
 rom Robin Williams\, Blondie and other now legendary rock bands. In the 
 ’80s as “Mubuhay Gardens” it was the epicenter of the San Francisco 
 punk scene with acts like the Go-Go’s\, The Dead Kennedys\, Iggy...\n\nF
 ree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/lights-on-tickets-20028918494
 38\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lights-sfs-historic-broadway-sign-rel
 ighting-sidewalk-party-north-beach/\nSource: Funcheap SF
