SUMMARY:Salvi Soul Encuentro 2026: SF’s Free Salvadoran Culture Festival
  (Oct 14-18)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1640321@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Salvi Soul Encuentro 2026: SF’s Free Salvadoran Culture Fest
 ival (Oct 14-18)\nSalvadoran Soul Encuentro\nSalvi Soul Encuentro is a fou
 r-date celebration of Salvadoran heritage in San Francisco’s Excelsior a
 nd Mission Districts. The program includes Salvadoran storytelling at Casa
  De Apoyo\, a poetry and vinyl record showcase\, a bike tour tracing the l
 egacy of Los Siete de la Raza\, and live outdoor performances at Excelsior
  and Mission\nIt’s going down this October 14-18th!\nSALVI SOUL ENCUENTR
 O 🇸🇻🎉\n\nCome join la fiesta as we navigate through the streets o
 f the Excelsior highlighting Salvadoran dance\, music\, poetry\, culture &
  community!\nFULL ITINERARY ⬇️\nWED OCT 14-SUN OCT 18\nSalvi Soul Encu
 entro\n10/14\nNiña Memita’s Kitchen Table\nNight of Salvadoran Storytel
 ling\n6PM I Casa De Apoyo 4834 Mission St\nThe festival officially kicks o
 ff on Wednesday\, October 14\, with Niña Memita’s Kitchen Table\, an in
 timate panel conversation about immigrant roots and local community legacy
 \, paired with a traditional Salvadoran menu from local\, woman-owned Andr
 ea’s Bakery.\n10/16\nLa Poesia es Como el Pan\, de Todos\nPoetry & Vinyl
  Record Showcase\n6PM I Casa De Apoyo\, 4834 Mission St\nThe celebration c
 ontinues on Friday with La Poesía es Como el Pan\, Para Todos\, a poetry 
 and vinyl listening party hosted by local author Norman Zelaya\, featuring
  confirmed spoken-word artists Karina Gamez and Mauricio Ramirez and DJ Ma
 joo\, alongside a community open mic.\n10/17\nRememberina Los Siete De La 
 Raza\nBike tour tracing t...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com
 /p/Ddt7OqOGmmZ/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&amp\;stkn=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==\nDe
 tails: https://sf.funcheap.com/salvi-soul-encuentro-2026-sfs-free-salvador
 an-culture-festival-oct-14-18/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/818583
 868_17904715530581104_3172970617812327818_n.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Casa De Apoyo\, 4834 Mission St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/salvi-soul-encuentro-2026-sfs-free-salvadoran-
 culture-festival-oct-14-18/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CRANE Watch Party: Shipyard Crane Light Show (Oct. 16-17)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T220000
DTSTAMP:20261014T120158Z
UID:funcheap-1642325@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:CRANE Watch Party: Shipyard Crane Light Show (Oct. 16-17)\nShi
 pyard Trust for the Arts\nThe historic gantry crane at Hunters Point Shipy
 ard comes to life in CRANE\, a large-scale work of public art in light\, o
 riginal music and projection. It honors the story of the Shipyard and Bayv
 iew Hunters Point\, and the people who built it\, worked it and lived it. 
 CRANE is the final event in the San Francisco Arts Commission’s Shaping 
 Legacy series.\nOn Friday\, October 16 and Saturday\, October 17\, watch t
 he performance from Building 101\, the Shipyard’s artist studio building
 \, more than half a mile across the Shipyard from the crane. The live feed
  from the crane is projected large on the building wall.\nCRANE Watch Part
 y\nFriday & Saturday\, October 16-17\, 2026\nBldg. 101\, Hunters Point Shi
 pyard\, 451 Galvez Ave.\, SF\nTickets: $10–$75\, with seated options in 
 Areas 1 and 2 and standing General Admission at $25. Bayview Hunters Point
  (94124) residents can enjoy a special $10 community ticket.\nIf ticket co
 sts are a barrier\, you can request financial assistance through this form
 .\nFULL SCHEDULE:\n\n5:30 pm Doors open\n6:00 pm Reception: Open Studios p
 review exhibition and art auction in the gallery\, food vendors and a bar 
 outside\, live jazz by Guitar Trifecta\n7:45 pm The Dr. George W. Davis Se
 nior Center Choir (live on Saturday\; on the livestream on Friday)\n8:00 t
 o 8:40 pm CRANE\nAfter the show\, the crane stays lit until 9:15 and the g
 allery stays open until 10:00\, with the artists back from the crane pier.
 ..\n\n$10.00\n\nTickets: https://shipyardartists.com/crane\nDetails: https
 ://sf.funcheap.com/crane-watch-party-shipyard-crane-light-show-oct-1617/\n
 Source: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CRANE_
 Funcheap_listing_Building101_1600x1280.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T120158Z
LOCATION:Hunters Point Shipyard\, Horn Ave\, Building 101\, San Francisco\
 , CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/crane-watch-party-shipyard-crane-light-show-oc
 t-1617/
END:VEVENT
