CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:FOSS is an immersive live audiovisual experience where electro
 nic music\, cinematic visuals\, and cutting-edge technology converge. Crea
 ted by Grammy-nominated pianist and composer Romain Collin and producer/el
 ectronic musician Jeremy Loucas\, the performance grew from Collin’s six
 -month artistic retreat in the remote Icelandic highlands\, where silence\
 , vast landscapes\, and isolation inspired a striking new creative vision.
 \n\nPerformed entirely live using modular synthesizers\, tape machines\, k
 eyboards\, and custom analog instruments—with no pre-recorded tracks—F
 OSS surrounds audiences with richly layered ambient soundscapes\, projecti
 on-mapped visuals\, and a quadraphonic sound system. The result is a mesme
 rizing\, genre-defying performance that blurs the boundaries between music
 \, film\, nature\, and technology.\n\nLearn more at fossfossfoss.com\n\n$3
 5\n\nTickets: https://gracecathedral.vbotickets.com/event/FOSS_an_immersiv
 e_live_audiovisual_experience/203642?utm_source=dothebay&utm_medium=calend
 ar&utm_campaign=foss\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/foss
 -an-immersive-live-audiovisual-experience-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
