SUMMARY:SF SHORT FILM FESTIVAL: Funny Shorts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T223000
DTSTAMP:20261013T170024Z
UID:dothebay-17947950@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:SF Short Film Festival presents:\n\nLAY LEFTY DOWN\n\nTwo wome
 n unexpectedly unite through stories of grief and laughter\, after their f
 amily throws a surprise memorial for a left breast.\n\nIT WAS AN ACCIDENT!
 \n\nConvinced he's accidentally killed a man at an orgy party\, a panicked
  young man enlists his best friend to help him deal with the body. As the 
 two scramble to figure out what to do next\, fear\, confusion\, and a comp
 lete lack of common sense lead them deeper into an increasingly absurd mes
 s.\n\nGLUE\n\nBlending sharp humor with emotional honesty\, GLUE follows a
  young woman who spends a single day working up the courage to have a conv
 ersation she’s been rehearsing in her head for weeks. It’s a heartfelt
  comedy about people-pleasing\, growing up\, and the terrifying — and li
 berating — act of finally saying what you really feel to the person you 
 love most.\n\nGOOGLE TRANSCRIPT\n\nTwo men in conflict are thrown into cha
 os when a new Google app recalls—and eventually predicts—their convers
 ations\, turning a petty disagreement into a confrontation they can't esca
 pe.\n\nHAWAII\n\nIn a near future where the elderly poor are rounded up in
  kill shelters like stray dogs\, a grumpy retiree forms an unexpected bond
  with the child who adopts him. Think "Black Mirror" meets Pixar's "Up".\n
 \nPARALLEL PROCESS\n\nA neurotic engineer fears AI is replacing his job an
 d life’s meaning\, while quirky friends and awkward dates push him to re
 discover his humanity.\n\nRESPAWN\n\nA man awakens in a mysterious open wo
 rld with no...\n\nTickets: https://sfshorts2026.eventive.org/schedule/6aac
 182d9bb2369fc4d530c6\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/16/sf-s
 hort-film-festival-funny-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
