SUMMARY:A Girl Walks Home Alone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T173000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17820764@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Strange things are afoot in Bad City. The Iranian ghost town\,
  home to prostitutes\, junkies\, pimps\, and other sordid souls\, is a pla
 ce that reeks of death and hopelessness\, where a lonely vampire is stalki
 ng the towns most unsavory inhabitants. But when boy meets girl\, an unusu
 al love story begins to blossom...blood red.\n\nThe first Iranian Vampire 
 Western\, Ana Lily Amirpour's debut feature A Girl Walks Home Alone at Nig
 ht basks in the sheer pleasure of pulp. A joyful mash-up of genre\, archet
 ype and iconography\, its prolific influences span spaghetti westerns\, gr
 aphic novels\, horror films\, and the Iranian New Wave. Amped by a mix of 
 Iranian rock\, techno and Morricone-inspired riffs\, its airy\, anamorphic
 \, black-and-white aesthetic and artfully drawn-out scenes combine the sim
 mering tension of Sergio Leone with the surrealism of David Lynch.\n\nPlay
 ing as part of the International Vampire Film Fest at the Balboa on Saturd
 ay\, October 17. Individual tickets and $30 day passes on sale now.\n\n$30
 \n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19830?siteToken=5
 2wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/17
 /a-girl-walks-home-alone-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
