UID:dothebay-17947940@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Green Film Festival presents:\n\nBIG RHONDA\n\nWhen a burnt ou
 t tech worker chases an influencer’s vision of off-grid freedom\, she in
 stead crashes into the harsh realities of van life and a new friendship th
 at challenges everything she thinks she knows about healing\, home\, and h
 ashtags.\n\nQ&A with filmmaker expected after the screening.\n\nCLIMATE CO
 NTROL\n\nA director making a documentary about fossil fuel extraction is c
 onsistently subverted by an AI agent that wants to tell a generic love sto
 ry.\n\nMade in collaboration with Gen Z film students at Cal Poly Humboldt
 \, the film looks at generational responses to the climate crisis through 
 an absurdist lens\, connecting the extraction of natural resources to the 
 extraction of our human data and the extraction of our attention in this p
 ost-information era.\n\nQ&A with filmmaker expected after the screening.\n
 \nTHE EPIC OF ENKIDU\n\nWhen the catastrophic king Gilgamesh meets the gra
 ss-fed Enkidu\, things don't go according to the clay tablets. A fractured
  take on the cuneiform tale\, featuring doom\, despair\, deception\, and s
 heep.\n\nOWED TO LAKE MERRITT\n\nVerna\, a traveling birder from the Midwe
 st\, comes to Oakland to see its bird sanctuary and immediately falls in l
 ove with Lake Merritt\, until a stranger opens her eyes to the deeper prob
 lems on its surface.\n\nQ&A with filmmaker expected after the screening.\n
 \nFISH-TWO-FISH\n\nBLUE and RED live trapped in a strange routine wearing 
 only pufferfish hats and underwear. They pass the time on a worn-out couch
 \,...\n\nTickets: https://greenfest2026.eventive.org/live_schedule/6aa42df
 687f30852901cfba2\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/19/green-f
 ilm-festival-narrative-fiction-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
