SUMMARY:SF SHORT FILM FESTIVAL: Spine-tingling Shorts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T201500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T221500
DTSTAMP:20261013T170024Z
UID:dothebay-17947937@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:SF Short Film Festival presents:\n\nKEEPSAKE\n\nWhen Lily’s 
 husband transports them back into their happiest memory together\, she mus
 t choose whether to face the harsh reality of their present or start over 
 in an idyllic past. The romantic gesture devolves into a surreal nightmare
  and Lily must find a way to save herself and her future.\n\nENTER\, MACHI
 NE\n\nThe short film is structured in three traditional acts\, yet shot al
 most entirely from the fixed perspective of a motionless red sedan that ne
 ver truly moves relative to the camera.\n\nThe audience feels as though st
 epping into a time machine\, witnessing three devastating tragedies unfold
 ing inside this single vehicle across different eras: Ryan’s joyful purc
 hase of his first car quickly collapses into family ruin amid financial ra
 ge and abandonment\; years (or moments) later\, Ian’s secret affair with
  Mary spirals into vehicular manslaughter after a rage-fueled chase kills 
 a food-stealing addict\; finally\, in a midnight forest\, a bound and mask
 ed Ryan brutally slays an unknown opponent in the back seat\, only for the
  car to lurch forward once in vain before snapping back to its original po
 sition—revealing the terrified original salesperson Hannah (kidnapped by
  Ryan) escaping from the trunk.\n\nThe film’s single futile movement del
 ivers a sharp satire on humanity’s illusion of progress trapped in an un
 changing cycle of destruction.\n\nI WILL COME TO YOU\n\nOrphaned as a baby
 \, Julian grows up in a Catholic boys’ home. As he uncovers his family
 ’...\n\nTickets: https://sfshorts2026.eventive.org/schedule/6aac189999c5
 1a7a44faa89b\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/20/sf-short-fil
 m-festival-spine-tingling-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34917152/deca68ce-a520-4791-9107-7b47cc900d39.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261013T170024Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/20/sf-short-film-festival-spine-ti
 ngling-shorts-tickets
