DESCRIPTION:Green Film Festival presents:\n\nFENCELINE: SHADOWS OVER THE R
 IVER PARISH\n\nFor generations\, families in Louisiana's River Parishes bu
 ilt communities along the Mississippi River. Many trace their roots to for
 merly enslaved people who settled the region after the Civil War\, establi
 shing churches\, schools\, farms\, and neighborhoods that remain today.\n\
 nNow surrounded by one of the largest petrochemical corridors in the world
 \, residents confront pollution\, illness\, industrial expansion\, and gro
 wing pressure on the places they call home.\n\nThrough the voices of those
  living on the frontlines of this industrial corridor\, Fenceline offers a
 n intimate portrait of communities determined to remain where their famili
 es have lived for generations.\n\nHYPERSCALED\n\nIncreased energy and wate
 r demands from the rapid development of large data centers driven by techn
 ological advancements like “AI”\, are increasing threats to communitie
 s across the Southeast. HYPERSCALED unearths the real world cost of AI as 
 residents fight to get answers about the costly impacts of this water and 
 energy sucking industry. Much like a vampire\, the proposed “Project Mar
 vel” is projected to consume unprecedented amounts of water and energy f
 rom the backyards of concerned communities.\n\nIN EARTH WE TRUST\n\nThe ri
 se and fall of the evangelical Reverend who nearly saved the planet. And h
 ow becoming a taxi driver influenced him to continue his mission of findin
 g common ground on the issue of climate change.\n\nFifteen years ago R...\
 n\nTickets: https://greenfest2026.eventive.org/live_schedule/6aa45daa68534
 f7eb2403f5d\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/21/green-film-fe
 stival-the-big-picture-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
