DESCRIPTION:SF Short Film Festival presents:\n\nTHE HAPPINESS INTERVENTION
 \n\nAn unlikely group of strangers travel to a remote retreat in Iceland\,
  one of the world's happiest countries\, each hoping to discover the secre
 t to a little happiness of their own.\n\nTHE SCHOOL PHOTOGRAPHER\n\nWith t
 he film industry in decline\, BJÖRN\, a seasoned first assistant director
 \, finds himself unemployed and adrift. To stay afloat\, he takes a tempor
 ary job as a school photographer—an unfamiliar and humbling role.\n\nOve
 r the course of one long day\, Björn’s fragile calm is tested by a stri
 ng of phone calls from his mother\, his teenage daughter\, and his ex-wife
 . Each conversation pulls him further off balance\, and the tension begins
  to seep into the portraits he takes. As his professional façade starts t
 o crack\, an unexpected encounter with a P.E. teacher at the school offers
  a brief moment of understanding—and a hint that change might still be p
 ossible.\n\nTHE FAMILY TREE\n\nAfter the passing of his wife\, Shelton is 
 left with a family heirloom\, a mysterious ancestral bonsai tree\, setting
  off a surreal encounter that blurs the line between life\, death\, and me
 mory.\n\nORNAMENTAL HORTICULTURE\n\nAfter experiencing the wrath of the in
 ternet firsthand\, an aspiring succulent influencer struggles to make her 
 second post.\n\nPUBERTY FOR HUMANS\n\nPuberty for Humans is perfect for yo
 ur nervous health class students as they approach their inevitable cyberne
 tic bodily changes. In this short educational video\, Linus\, an insecure 
 prepubes...\n\nTickets: https://sfshorts2026.eventive.org/schedule/6aac17d
 a8c39bc3779dbc104\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/21/sf-shor
 t-film-festival-closing-night-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
