DTSTAMP:20261013T170024Z
UID:dothebay-17947934@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Green Film Festival presents:\n\nA CITY IN THE FOREST\n\n(Clos
 ing Night Film)\n\nWhen a private police foundation in Atlanta tries to ra
 ze an urban forest to build the country’s largest police training facili
 ty\, a diverse\, decentralized\, and intersectional movement defends the f
 orest from what they call “Cop City.” A City in the Forest paints a co
 llective portrait of the country’s most urgent social justice story\, wh
 ere a web of activists fight back against environmental racism\, political
  corruption\, police violence\, and the criminalization of dissent.\n\nFor
 get the guilt trip\, the Green Film Festival of San Francisco\, the mischi
 evous\, tree-hugging cousin of the 29 year old SF IndieFest\, returns Oct 
 15-22 to prove that saving the planet doesn't have to feel like homework. 
 We've ditched the doom-and-gloom documentaries that make you want to crawl
  under a (sustainably sourced) blanket and never come out. The line-up thi
 s year pairs sharp environmental storytelling with wit\, weirdness\, and u
 napologetic irreverence. And yes\, our Eco-Horror midnight movie is back!\
 n\nWhether you’re an eco-curious cinephile or a die-hard activist\, come
  join in the fun because if we're going to talk about the end of the world
  as we know it\, we might as well laugh\, gasp\, and maybe even dance a li
 ttle on the way there. Through this experience the festival hopes audience
 s can begin to engage with sustainable solutions to the problems facing th
 e planet.\n\nTickets: https://greenfest2026.eventive.org/live_schedule/6a9
 eecde94df30d1f91604e3\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/22/gre
 en-film-festival-a-city-in-the-forest-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
