SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:(((folkYEAH!))) presents:\n\nNOSFERATU: A SYMPHONY OF HORROR\n
 \n(F.W. Murnau\, 1922)\n\nThe mysterious Count Orlok summons a happily mar
 ried real estate agent to his castle\, located up in the Transylvanian mou
 ntains\, to finalise a terrifying deal.\n\nwith LIVE ORIGINAL SCORE perfor
 med by\n\nPaz Lenchantin\n\nPaz Lenchantin is a musician best known for pl
 aying bass in such varied groups as Pixies\, Zwan\, A Perfect Circle\, Sil
 ver Jews\, and the Entrance Band. In addition to bass\, she sings\, plays 
 piano\, violin\, guitar\, and drums. She played strings on Queens of the S
 tone Age’s Songs For the Deaf\, Melissa Auf der Maur’s first solo albu
 m\, and for several scenes in Michael Mann’s 2006 film\, Miami Vice. Len
 chantin also directed the music video for Pixies’ “Human Crime.” Her
  debut solo album\, Triste\, was released in October 2025 on her own label
 \, Hideous Humans Records. —The Creative Independent\n\nSpotify | IG\n\n
 Dallas Acid\n\nDallas Acid is a synth-heavy dreampop trio from Austin\, Te
 xas and the first new signing to All Saints Records in a number of years. 
 Following previous releases on Flying Moonlight and Olde English Spelling 
 Bee\, they join a roster that includes Brian Eno\, Harold Budd and Laraaji
  (who the band previously collaborated with on 2018’s Arrive Without Lea
 ving album).\n\nAll Saints Records founder Dominic Norman-Taylor comments:
  “Dallas Acid's unique mix of minimalist electronic music with a big bal
 lad sensibility creates gorgeous\, utterly compelling immersive soundworld
 s. All Saints Reco...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purch
 ase/19681?siteToken=d2atbcege5knqsavntt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.
 com/events/2026/10/23/nosferatu-a-symphony-of-horror-with-live-score-by-da
 llas-acid-paz-lenchantin-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33899578/2c4824aa-f136-4027-886b-6829cf9baa08.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/23/nosferatu-a-symphony-of-horror-
 with-live-score-by-dallas-acid-paz-lenchantin-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: Izaak Opatz\, Joe Kaplow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17731649@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Izaak Opatz\n\nIzaak Opatz’s music has always been about lon
 ging\, run through with nostalgia for the passed-by and out-of-reach. His 
 first two albums\, Mariachi Static and Extra Medium\, were propelled by a 
 longing for specific people and places\, made relatable by wry humor\, tho
 ughtful simile and close observation.\n\nMore recently\, he’s been writi
 ng songs that long for an alternative reality\, for different possibilitie
 s than the short\, doomed menu offered by our tech lords and the current k
 akistocracy failing to regulate them. Songs that push back against the coe
 rcive pressure to indulge in small conveniences at the expense of personal
  privacy\, a 20th-century attention span and the steady drip of a monthly 
 subscription:\n\nI spend a lot of my time now\, jumping through hoops / as
 king permission from a little screen convincing a robot that I’m not a r
 obot / this future isn’t all it was cracked up to be\n\nJoe Kaplow\n\nMy
  music comes from life’s moments — smelling 4 acres of freshly cut gra
 ss\, watching the steam from a horse’s breath in the early morning\, fin
 ally holding the neck of my guitar after holding bridles and worn wooden h
 andles all day. 4000 acres of freshly burnt wildfire\, watching the steam 
 from the Pacific Ocean’s breath in the early morning\, finally holding t
 he neck of my guitar after clutching the worn steering wheel of the tour v
 an all day.\n\nNow my reality is in Bonny Doon\, CA\, where mountains meet
  the sea. I am in my recording studio\, aptly named Hippie Cowboy\, every 
 day....\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19672?site
 Token=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/202
 6/10/23/live-music-izaak-opatz-joe-kaplow-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33899680/77d37564-21ef-4481-8ec8-95f4f5c5c967.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/23/live-music-izaak-opatz-joe-kapl
 ow-tickets
END:VEVENT
