BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:My Benjamin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17882147@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Dance
DESCRIPTION:A visual essay on the loving acceptance of what comes to an en
 d\, starring Paris Opera Ballet Étoile Benjamin Pech.\n\nMy Benjamin foll
 ows Benjamin Pech during his final year as an Étoile at the Paris Opera B
 allet\, tracing the arc of his artistic life inside the storied Palais Gar
 nier\, from his entry into the Opera’s ballet school at age ten to the s
 evere hip injury that now threatens to end his career.\n\nAlong the way\, 
 director Victoria Clay Mendoza and Pech develop an unexpected friendship i
 n which each sees themselves reflected in the other: as Pech confronts a b
 ody that can no longer sustain him\, Clay Mendoza faces her own return to 
 Mexico to care for her mother\, who has been diagnosed with Alzheimer’s.
 \n\nA visual essay on endings\, on the loving acceptance of deterioration\
 , and on the need to be seen through these processes\, My Benjamin renders
  the private world of ballet intimate and immediate\, following Benjamin
 ’s daily routine with rare access and tenderness.\n\nFollowed by a live 
 Q&A with director Victoria Clay Mendoza\, moderated by Sabrina Bot (MerciS
 F).\n\n20-40\n2026 SF Dance Film Festival:\n\nTickets: https://sfdancefilm
 fest.org/fall-festival-2026/my-benjamin/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/ev
 ents/2026/10/29/my-benjamin-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7843591;-122.3885501
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34611137/b6a13e24-868e-4486-85e3-3297bb808c5d.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Delancey Street Screening Room\, 600 The Embarcadero\, San Franci
 sco\, CA\, 94107
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/29/my-benjamin-tickets
